/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.local

# Editor
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
.claude/

# grizzly-gate local report output
grizzly-gate-report/

# Vendored semgrep rules (gh#320): reproduced from the pinned image by
# `just vendor-semgrep`, hashed by `just check-vendored`, read by
# `just scan-semgrep`. Git-ignored because the tree carries semgrep test
# fixtures that are not JSON, which the pre-commit duplicate-key guard
# refuses to commit. Never hand-edit; re-vendor instead.
gate-semgrep-rules/

# Frontend
web/node_modules
web/dist/

# grizzly-gate local toolchain install dir
web/.grizzly-gate.node_modules/
.pr-body.md
__pycache__/

# Host-path contamination (AGENTS.md "Tool output never goes to a host path").
# A host path whose leading `/` is lost lands in the tree as a top-level
# `home/…`, `tmp/…` or `paperclip/…` directory. These entries are anchored at
# the worktree root and cover only that shape. Coverage limit: top-level
# `home/`, `tmp/`, `paperclip/` only — no bare `.tmp/` basename pattern (that
# would also hide a real directory named `tmp` at any depth) and no
# depth-threshold scrub (that misses shallow paths). These entries do not
# prevent contamination; the AGENTS.md clause is the control. They only stop
# the known shape from being swept into a commit by `git add -A`/`commit -a`.
/home/
/.tmp/
/.paperclip/
